// ===================== 3.5 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('3.5  Two of the three points, and why those two'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **Enforce the rule that no two students may give the same ground.** **It sounds like a game and it is the only way to get ten grounds out of a room** — **left alone, eight of the ten say _the most important_.** **Then let the room say which of the ten it would read, and count the votes against the grounds that name a property.**'));
out.push(A('**b** A ground: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **Not 1** (_interest me most_), **not 3** (_the most important_), **not 5** (_in the time available_, which is about the page). **Read 5 aloud and ask what it tells a reader about the two chosen points.** **Nothing at all** — **it is the formula of 3.1 arriving in a new place.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — **that it names a property the two chosen points share and the third does not**, so a reader can check the choice rather than agree with it.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** **How the ten minutes affect teaching time; how many families are affected; and whether the change should be adopted across the governorate.** ⚠ **He answered the first two** — **the third is a policy question and he runs one school.** **2** ⚠ **It is not a property of the questions at all but an opinion about them**, and a reader who disagrees has nothing to disagree with, which means they simply think you chose the easy two.'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The test in this cycle is one question and it should go on the board in those words: can the ground be wrong?** **_Answerable from this school\'s own records_ can be wrong — somebody may show that the third is answerable too.** **_The most important_ cannot be wrong and therefore cannot be checked.** **A ground that cannot be wrong is a preference with a long word in front of it.** ⚠ **Run Stage 4b as a real attempt and not as a formality: the partner has to try to make the ground wrong, in one sentence, and about a third of the grounds in any room fall over.** **A ground that survives one attempt is a ground.** **This is the same move as the unrolling test in 1.3 and the class should be told so** — **both of them work by converting something that feels like judgement into something that can be shown to be false.**'));
