out.push(A('⚠ Mark these on **whether the ground could be wrong.** **Item 4 is the one to teach hardest**, because it is the ground that writes the essay: **two points that cannot both be true give you an argument before the first word, and two points that agree give you four hundred words of saying the same thing twice.** **Item 5 is the honest fallback and students should be told it is allowed** — **a set of three testable points genuinely has no property-based ground, and inventing one is worse than admitting a choice.**'));
